{"action_id":"action.8ffdbace18ea4e1da3443646b5b419e8","provenance":{"allowance_slot":60,"cli_version":"codex-cli 0.153.4","configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0ce5b-96e5-70c2-b9b8-66f189928676\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as the US transition date and business-day cycle, with the Canada footnote qualifying Transition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as the general LC assessment and proportionate operational-measures expectation.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as the readiness expectation governing the following examples.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted through competing geographic readings of the selected liquidity control; FX remains T+2.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as staffing availability and training expectations with discretionary implementation methods.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as proactive communication directed to potentially affected clients.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Separate fund-management actor scope; considerable US exposure is emphasized, not stated as an exclusive threshold.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Fund-specific impact assessment is outside the selected LC operational control; it identifies subscription and non-US proceeds dependencies.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"DEFERRED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Fund-specific arrangements where necessary are outside the selected control; illustrative additional staffing does not impose an LC-wide staffing method.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"DEFERRED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Fund-specific early alerts and remedial actions are outside the selected control and are not imported into LC client communication.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"DEFERRED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"SFC monitoring statement supplies context rather than an LC operational requirement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional signature text.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional signature text.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Institutional signature text.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Illustrative securities categories, not an exhaustive definition or independent statement of product-specific settlement rules.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expressly includes Canada in Transition and supplies its distinct effective date.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Non-exhaustive examples of post-trade processes inform staffing readiness.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"LCs are the selected actors. Potentially affected clients delimit communication recipients. Fund management companies have additional separately addressed expectations. The geographic reach of the expressly US-worded liquidity example supports competing readings.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Transition expressly includes the US and Canada. T+1 and T+2 concern business-day settlement intervals; the securities and post-trade lists are illustrative.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"No blanket exemption is supplied. 'where appropriate' leaves uncertainty about whether it qualifies only staffing arrangements or the whole list of enhancements. It does not clearly waive assessment, readiness, timely funding, or staff availability.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'should', 'ensuring', and 'may consider' distinguish supervisory expectations and outcomes from optional means. The packet does not establish their independent legal enforceability.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"US transition: 2024-05-28; Canada: 2024-05-27. Preparation is anticipatory and operations must remain effective after transition. No exact assessment, training, or client-contact deadline is supplied. FX remains T+2.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Readiness depends on liquidity, funding timing, staffing, training and operational processes. Cross-currency funding requires attention to the securities/FX cycle mismatch. Calendar conventions, operational cutoffs and adequacy criteria are not supplied.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the Canada-inclusive definition extend the expressly US-worded liquidity example to Canadian transactions, or does Canada remain covered through the general readiness expectation?\\\",\\n    \\\"Does 'where appropriate' qualify only staffing arrangements or all listed enhancements?\\\",\\n    \\\"What operational cutoffs, business-day calendars and evidence establish timely funding, adequate training and readiness?\\\",\\n    \\\"What legal force attaches to these supervisory expectations? The supplied packet alone does not resolve that question.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The expressly US-worded liquidity example is read literally; Canada's inclusion still governs the general Transition readiness expectation.\\\",\\\"The Boolean result evaluates only the selected liquidity control within scope and does not determine overall compliance.\\\"],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"For cross-currency transactions, given that the standard settlement cycle for foreign-exchange transactions remains at T+2, LCs should be mindful of potential liquidity mismatches and settlement failures arising from the different settlement cycles for US securities and foreign-exchange transactions;\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"The specific liquidity example expressly tests US transactions. Canadian readiness remains relevant under the general provision, but is not an additional condition of this selected test. The strongest uncertainty is how the broader defined Transition interacts with repeated US-specific wording.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed entity is a licensed corporation.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_lc\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC's business involves US securities settlements affected by the Transition.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"us_affected\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC's business involves Canadian securities settlements affected by the Transition.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"canada_affected\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"For the affected US business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"us_liquidity_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"For the affected Canadian business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"canada_liquidity_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"us_liquidity_ready\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_lc us_affected)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"liquidity_us_literal\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\\"Is the US-specific example intentionally narrower than the defined Transition?\\\"],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For an LC with affected US settlement business, true means the selected US liquidity readiness expectation is met: liquidity practices are reviewed, necessary funding is available on time, and cross-currency mismatch risks are considered where relevant. FX T+2 is a dependency, not an exemption or a requirement to change FX to T+1.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"LC liquidity readiness: literal geographic reach\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The US liquidity example expresses an operational expectation that also applies to affected Canadian settlements through the expressly Canada-inclusive Transition.\\\",\\\"The Boolean result evaluates only this broader selected liquidity control, not overall compliance.\\\"],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"LCs should assess their readiness and ensure they are able to cope with the shortened settlement cycle, including:\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"2 The settlement cycle in Canada will transition to T+1 on 27 May 2024. The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"An LC affected only in Canada enters scope, and an LC affected in both markets must satisfy liquidity readiness for both. This gains support from the defined Transition and inclusive readiness introduction, but requires extending the expressly US-worded example; that extension is the strongest uncertainty.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed entity is a licensed corporation.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_lc\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC's business involves US securities settlements affected by the Transition.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"us_affected\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC's business involves Canadian securities settlements affected by the Transition.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"canada_affected\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"For the affected US business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"us_liquidity_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"For the affected Canadian business, liquidity practices have been reviewed, necessary funding is available for timely securities settlement, and any cross-currency cycle mismatch and resulting failure risk have been considered.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"canada_liquidity_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"(and (if us_affected us_liquidity_ready true) (if canada_affected canada_liquidity_ready true))\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_lc (or us_affected canada_affected))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"liquidity_transition_wide\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\\"Is extending the liquidity example to Canada justified by the defined term despite the specific US references?\\\"],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For an LC with affected US or Canadian settlement business, true means the selected Transition-wide liquidity readiness expectation is met for each affected market: liquidity review, timely funding, and consideration of relevant cross-currency mismatch risks. Canada transitions on 2024-05-27 and the US on 2024-05-28; the FX cycle remains T+2.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"LC liquidity readiness: Transition-wide geographic reach\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Outcome expectations and optional implementation suggestions retain their different modalities.\\\",\\\"Adequacy and timeliness require assessment against the LC's relevant operations; no fixed headcount or training duration is supplied.\\\"],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Ensuring the availability of staff to complete the post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"LCs may consider adjusting their staff’s work shifts, extending working hours or arranging evening or morning duties in conjunction with automating their operational processes to enable timely trade settlements.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Adequate training should be provided to enable relevant staff to effectively perform their duties under the shortened settlement cycle;\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"3 Including trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Staff availability and adequate training are expected outcomes. Shift changes, longer hours, evening or morning duties and the associated automation suggestion are discretionary means; choosing none does not itself fail the control. The strongest uncertainty concerns operational adequacy, not whether a particular shift pattern is mandatory.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":null,\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"staffing_outcomes\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\\"What evidence establishes sufficient availability and adequate training for all relevant post-trade processes?\\\"],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected staffing readiness control is satisfied when staff are available to complete relevant post-trade processes within the shortened timeframe and relevant staff receive adequate training for effective performance. The listed staffing adjustments are optional measures to consider. Trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation are included examples, not the complete process list.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"LC staffing availability and training\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The reminder addresses LCs generally for impact assessment; appropriate operational changes depend on their business impact.\\\",\\\"The exact attachment of 'where appropriate' remains unresolved.\\\",\\\"The qualitative adequacy and preparation timing requirements are retained without inventing numerical thresholds.\\\"],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"the SFC wishes to remind licensed corporations (LCs) to assess the impact of the Transition on their businesses and take appropriate measures to maintain their smooth and effective operations after the Transition.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"These include enhancing their operational processes, technological infrastructure and systems as well as staffing arrangements where appropriate.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Proactively engaging and communicating with their clients who are potentially affected by the Transition in order to raise their awareness and facilitate their preparations for a smooth transition.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Effective 28 May 2024, the standard settlement cycle for transactions in US securities1 will be shortened from two business days after the trade date (T+2) to one business day after trading (T+1) (the Transition)2.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Such as equities, bonds, exchange-traded funds and options.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Assessment is addressed generally to LCs, while changes depend on appropriateness and communication targets potentially affected clients. A narrow grammatical attachment makes only staffing enhancements expressly conditional; a broader attachment makes all listed enhancements expressly conditional. Neither reading supplies a blanket exemption from assessing impact or being ready.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":null,\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"assessment_and_preparation\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\\"Does 'where appropriate' attach solely to staffing arrangements or to the whole enhancement list?\\\",\\\"How early must communication occur to facilitate client preparations?\\\",\\\"Which specific securities transactions fall within the standard-cycle change? The illustrative product list does not resolve every transaction.\\\"],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected LC assessment and preparation control is satisfied when the LC assesses the US and Canadian Transition's business impact, takes appropriate measures to maintain smooth and effective operations afterward, and proactively engages potentially affected clients to support awareness and preparation. Securities examples are non-exhaustive. The effective dates describe market transitions, not a newly invented start date for preparation duties.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"LC impact assessment, proportionate enhancements and client preparation\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":30948,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":5127,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":69}}\n","fresh_context":true,"independence":"CONTEXT_ONLY_SAME_MODEL_CORRELATION_UNMEASURED","model":"gpt-6-astra","provider":"codex.fresh.v1","provider_route_hash":"3d676052ff208